<Shell title="Open from hardware to apps">
<section class="frame page-heading"><span class="micro">The open-source direction</span><h1>Open from<br />the board up.</h1><p>The hardware, the firmware and the apps are all part of the system you depend on. Our direction is to make each layer inspectable, adaptable and maintainable.</p></section>
<section class="frame page-body"><div class="feature-rows"><article id="hardware"><h3>Understand the hardware.</h3><p>Editable board and enclosure designs give owners and builders a way to see how the system is made. Hardware design files are present in the working project; the public package and hardware licence still need to be established.</p></article><article id="firmware"><h3>Inspect the control logic.</h3><p>Local decisions should be understandable from source. The Rust workspace declares MIT OR Apache-2.0. A public source release and complete licence files still need verification before download links can be offered here.</p></article><article id="apps"><h3>Adapt the way you use it.</h3><p>The open-stack plan includes the Offgrid app and the interfaces around it. The current website shows proposed screens; an app source release and its licence are still to be confirmed.</p></article><article><h3>Extend equipment connections.</h3><p>Documented profiles and interfaces can help contributors add equipment over time. The catalogue preserves research evidence and uncertainty; a new integration still needs implementation and validation.</p></article></div>
<section class="subsection"><span class="micro">Source & release status / 07 September 2026</span><h2>Make the promise inspectable.</h2><p>Origin89 is in development. This table makes the current release work visible alongside the open-source direction.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Open stack release status"><table class="source-table"><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Present in the project</th><th>Public-release work</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Hardware</th><td>PCB source, mechanical files and editable enclosure CAD</td><td>Choose and publish the hardware licence and release package</td></tr><tr><th>Firmware / Rust core</th><td>Source and a workspace MIT OR Apache-2.0 declaration</td><td>Complete licence files and verify public repository access</td></tr><tr><th>Offgrid & Buddy</th><td>Product definitions and website interface concepts</td><td>Confirm app source, scope, licences and release links</td></tr><tr><th>Equipment catalogue</th><td>Model entries, protocol research and confidence notes</td><td>Connect published support status to actual driver and hardware evidence</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="small-note">The repository URL declared in the workspace did not resolve publicly during this review. Source-download links will belong here once the release is accessible.</p></section></section><CTA />
</Shell>
